<title>UK: St. Ives says strong stg could hurt results.</title>
<headline>St. Ives says strong stg could hurt results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>British printing group St. Ives Plc said on Tuesday that if sterling stayed strong, it would continue to weigh on its results.</p>
<p>However, the company, posting a 20 percent rise in first-half pretax profits, said the overall outlook remained encouraging in Britain and overseas.</p>
<p>&quot;The current momentum of our business enables us to look forward to another satisfactory outcome for the year as a whole,&quot; the firm said in a statement.</p>
</text>
